<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann to seek Luxembourg phone license.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann to seek Luxembourg phone license.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mannesmann AG said on Tuesday it planned to apply for a license to provide mobile phone service in Luxembourg through a venture called Luxcall.</p>
<p>Its Mannesmann Eurokom GmbH unit holds a 35 percent stake in Luxcall, while Compagnie Luxembourgeoise de Telecomunications (CL-COM) owns 51 percent and Compagnie Generale de Services et d'Applications de Telecommunications SA (CGSAT) has 14 percent.</p>
<p>CL-COM is partly owned by Cegedel, Luxembourg's partly privatised electric utility.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
